en is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a superficial 0 3cm rim of tan white fibrosis  with admixed lobules of fat necrosis up to 0 3cm in diameter  underlying the superior aspect of the entire specimen  The remainder of the specimen consists almost entirely of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  with only scant tan white fibrous breast parenchyma identified  No masses or focal lesions are identified  The specimen is entirely and sequentially submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the medial tip en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the lateral tip en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  final margin left breast   are four unoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue  with focal fibrosis and cautery  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no masses or focal lesions  The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 28   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 31 14PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left  Re  Excision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin   Excision  report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
