ive percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two specimens  Labeled  Lumpectomy  breast cancer site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm mass with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm that has a 4 1cm healed scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hard  stellate  white mass intermixed with yellow chalky areas  The central portion of the stellate mass contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm dark brown elliptical focus  The mass is 0 4cm from its closest margin  Labeled  Right axillary node  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm mass of adipose tissue with intermixed lymph nodes  Dissection reveals multiple lymph nodes that are entirely submitted  Section Code  A D  representative sections of the mass  E  closest resection margin  F J  axillary lymph nodes  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODES  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST MASS  RIGHT    report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
