cm in diameter with inverted nipple and 2 5cm curvilinear scar in the superior medial aspect of the areolar  skin border  A long suture designates the lateral aspect and a short suture designates the superior aspect of the specimen  The external surface is lobulated  unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a white  stellate  gritty area beneath the nipple areolar complex running into rubbery  white pink breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in greatest dimension and extending to 3 5cm of the deep margin  No biopsy cavity is identified  however  a bright yellow  gritty material surrounding this area suggesting a biopsy site  Multiple other foci of fibrous  white pink breast tissue without specific nodules are present throughout the specimen  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  the largest REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  SECTION CODE  A C  representative sections of the white  gray  stellate area under the areola  D F  representative adjacent breast tissue  G K  representative sections of the deep margin  L P  representative sections of breast tissue from medial to lateral  Q T  axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  Right axillary tissue   is a fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a lymph node  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The lymph node is sectioned and submitted in cassette U  The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted in cassette V  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  SOFT TISSUE  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
