Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 34 CLINICAL DATA  Hypoechoic mass 2 o clock left breast r o malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  2 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSIES  FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE ADDENDUM  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains there is no staining of tumor cells  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in a follicular pattern  The B cells are positive for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The tumor cells are also positive for bcl 2 and focally for Ki 67  approximately 10    The tumor cells are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of follicular lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  are 2 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A  Gross Description by  JIM BRADLEY Resident  WEN JING  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Elizabeth A Rafferty  M D  Charles Harris Weiss  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  2 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSIES , Core_biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 98 at 14 37 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  14 MAY 98 at 17 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft tan cores of tissue  submitted in toto in Cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Annekathryn Goodman  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Core_biopsy.
