Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 23 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  1cm in greatest dimension  extending to 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen  INFILTRATING PAPILLARY CARCINOMA  1 2cm in greatest dimension  extending to 2cm from the posterior margin of the specimen  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  No tumor remains in the region of the biopsy site  The two remaining nodules appear anatomically discrete and histoclogically dissimilar  Several centimeters of unremarkable breast parenchyma separates each from the area of the previous procedure  The papillary growth pattern of one nodule makes evaluation of the extent of invasion difficult  but I believe that most of the tumor in this mass represents invasive carcinoma  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  solid and cribriform types  involving ducts and lobules in six of twelve sections from the region of the biopsy cavity and surrounding parenchyma  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Invasion of stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear negative  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERFICIAL NODULE  SLIDE O  DEEP NODULE  SLIDE V   THE TUMOR CELLS IN BOTH NODULES STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS IN BOTH NODULES STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 94 at 11 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen comprises two portions  The first portion represents a left simple mastectomy specimen  A fully healed surgical scar spans about 2cm and originates 1 5cm from the nipple  Posterior to the scar sits a 1cm cavity containing bloody fluid  A rim of firm yellow white tissue 0 1cm thick surrounds the space  The adjacent parenchyma and the remainder of the tissue in the breast appear unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A   D Tissue adjacent to the cavity E   L Cavity M   N Tissue from the tail of the breast The second portion represents a right modified radical mastectomy specimen displaying a completely healed 2 5cm scar  The tissue posterior to the scar looks mottled yellow  white  and gray  and it feels firm  No cavity or mass remains in this region  Posterior to this location one finds two nodules  The deepest appears irregular  ill defined  and yellow and white  It spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and extends no closer than 1cm to the deep margin  Slightly anterior to this nodule one finds a well defined  lobulated mass of soft  granular  red and tan tissue that has dimensions of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and extends to about 2cm from the margin of the specimen  The remainder of the parenchyma looks unremarkable  SECTION CODE  O   P Deepest nodule Q   T Tissue adjacent to deep margin and deep nodule U   V More superficial nodule W  AA Region of prior biopsy BB HH Axillary tissue Resident  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  Janey Pratt  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART B  LEFT BREAST   report_end  , No_breast_biopsy.
